cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research framework, please cite this repository using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "D-BTP: Dynamic Bucket Tree of Permutation — Directional Structural Generation and Hypothesis Evolution"
authors:
  - family-names: Tan
    given-names: Sizhe
abstract: >-
  D-BTP is a research framework for dynamic structural hypothesis search.
  It integrates state-dependent candidate generation, constraint-guided
  structural composition, directional generation and selection, weak-evidence
  exploration, feedback, and optional multi-agent structural relay.
  The repository presents theoretical foundations, interface contracts,
  application cases, and proposed validation protocols; empirical advantages
  and recursive self-improvement are research hypotheses, not established results.
keywords:
  - dynamic structural search
  - bucket tree of permutation
  - structural intelligence
  - directional fields
  - weak evidence
  - constraint-guided search
  - multi-agent learning
  - structural relay
license: Apache-2.0
